WEBVTT

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.650
Sophie-chan!

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.420
It's nighttime.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.610
Aren't you going to get up?

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.070
Five more minutes.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.120
<i>My name is Amano Akari.</i>

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.830
<i>I'm a regular girl in high school, 
living with a vampire.</i>

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.850
When she's like this, she really 
does look just like a doll.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.190
She doesn't breathe, no body 
warmth, and she never ages.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.660
Vampires sure are great.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.930
<i>My friends often say that 
my tastes are quite unique.</i>

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.170
You're really not getting up?

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.260
I'll play a trick on you if you don't.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.240
Good morning.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:46.980
You got up!

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.950
Why are you so surprised?

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.570
Didn't you come to wake me up?

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.740
No reason.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.210
Something's fishy here.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:00.150
No, everything's just fine!

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:04.460
Did you doodle something on my face?

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.440
<b>Meat</b>

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.760
Of course not!

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.570
See?

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:10.420
Um, that doesn't work for me.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.210
Well, whatever. Sorry for doubting you.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:17.150
Huh?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.200
Don't do my hair without asking!

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.530
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:57.530
<b>Akari's Friend</b>

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.050
<b>Celebrating 3 Million Copies Sold & The Release of Volume 8
The autograph session with Surume-sensei is finally this Sunday!</b>

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.050
It's Tough 
Putting Up with 
My Little Sister 
And My Mom

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.490
It's finally tomorrow.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.350
But the book signing is during the day.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.030
You'll turn into a pile of ash 
if you go out in the sun.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.350
Isn't that dangerous?

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.870
Not if I go in prepared.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.400
Like using a parasol,

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.630
or a cloak.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.130
I see.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.860
And if I write a will just 
in case, I'll be even safer.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:24.640
"My computer's hard drive is to be destroyed 
without inspection of its content."

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.850
Is this really going to be okay?

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.580
Wow, you have so many!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.860
Collecting signed books is a 
hobby I've had for a long time.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.220
I collected them all myself.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.530
These all look really old.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.150
That's Poe's autograph.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.430
Wow.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.290
Wait, Poe was alive over a 
hundred years ago, right?

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.250
How old are you again?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.960
Well... It's ten and some years 
into the 21st century now...

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.880
So that would be around 360...

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.700
No, wait! That's a secret!

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.160
Don't you know it's rude to ask a girl's age?

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.750
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:11.140
<i>I guess even 360-some-year-olds 
are self-conscious about that.</i>

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.910
Even when the author dies, 
their works live on.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.460
Getting a book you've read 
while its author is still alive signed

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.110
makes the book a sort of memento.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.150
There are a lot of books here 
that nobody knows anymore,

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.800
but for me, they're all full of memories.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.800
It's a wonderful collection.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:33.360
You forget a lot of things 
when you get as old as me,

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.430
but when I pick up one of 
these books, I remember it

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.630
as if I read it yesterday.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:41.690
Like the day I got this book signed...

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.640
I remember that the author wasn't 
anything like I had imagined.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.830
<b>Macho</b>

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.510
That a dog barked at me on the way home.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.100
<b>Bark</b>

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:48.470
<b>Pour</b>

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.760
That I got caught in a rainstorm.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.680
<b>Pour</b>

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:50.760
<b>Pour</b>

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.230
A surprising lack of pleasant memories...

00:04:55.170 --> 00:05:00.230
I guess humans and vampires experience 
time in a very different span.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:03.990
You're 360 years old, huh? 
That's a little surprising.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.540
Forget about my age already.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.620
Can't you just consider me forever thirteen?

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:11.910
Being able to see lots of 
different eras sounds nice,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.110
but it must be hard to watch 
friends and lovers

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:17.020
who were born after you 
pass away before you do.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.040
Akari...

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.750
You're very wrong to assume that 
everybody has friends and lovers.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.650
Sophie-chan, you have me!

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.840
Cheer up!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:33.010
<i>I didn't expect such a depressing answer.</i>

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:41.070
<i>I'd better use a parasol, 
cloak, and some gloves.</i>

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:45.530
<i>It's a sunny day, so I need to be very mindful.</i>

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.830
Good morning, Sophie-chan.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.370
Morning.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.080
Intruder?!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.680
All right, I'm ready to go!

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.520
I've got my parasol and cloak, 
so the sun doesn't scare me!

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.670
Wait!

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.670
I need to get ready!

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.180
The weather's so nice.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.880
Look at these cute flowers.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:20.150
Sophie-chan?

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.480
Are you okay, Sophie-chan?

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.190
I lied. I'm scared.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.090
I see.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:32.660
You can prepare, but you can't 
get rid of that fear, huh?

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:37.410
This weather is nice for me, 
but for you, it's horrible.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:38.790
Akari...

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.710
Don't leave my side.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:42.800
<i>What?!</i>

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.670
<i>Is she depending on me?!</i>

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:48.530
Don't worry! I'll stay with 
you for the rest of my life!

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:51.340
Actually, why don't you step 
back fifty centimeters?

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.910
Maybe you could look into 
some UV-blocking creams?

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.980
They didn't really work.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.720
So you've already tried it.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.630
I also tried UV-blocking 
contacts and treatments.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.540
Look, birds!

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:24.890
<i>We could have easily left much later. 
She must be really excited.</i>

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:27.710
Huh?

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.510
It's shorter if we go this way.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:35.050
But there's a gyoza shop in that 
direction, and the garlic smell...

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.060
If we turn here, it's...

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.790
That goes along a river, 
though, so I'd rather not.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.650
I don't like running water.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:44.050
What about this way?

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:45.360
There's a church.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.700
This street looks fine.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.350
The four-eyed dog is here!

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:56.630
Let's retreat for now.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:57.830
The four-eyed dog?

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:02.300
I'm starting to think we 
might not make it in time.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.380
We're almost there!

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.050
Come to think of it, 
this is the first time we've ever

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.790
gone out somewhere on my day off.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.410
It's like we're on a date or something.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:19.640
Really?

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.120
D-Does it bother you that much?

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.970
No, I'm just a little tired.

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:31.160
Being under the sun makes my energy 
drop down to <i>Spe*unker</i> levels.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.860
Oh, good.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:37.290
Well, we still have some time, 
so why don't we take a break?

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.440
This is perfect.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:43.970
It's in the shade, too.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.970
The wind feels nice.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:53.460
The light filtering through the 
leaves is so sparkly and pretty.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.200
You're right.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:02.470
Sophie-chan, it's turning you to ash!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.500
I guess even under the trees isn't safe.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.460
Maybe we should go in somewhere.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.050
Let's go in there!

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:15.240
<i>Oh, right... Sophie-chan only drinks blood.</i>

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.930
<b>Rich</b>

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:15.200
<b>Tasty</b>

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.140
Maybe we should find another place.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.990
Wait, that's the stuff high school 
girls in anime are always eating!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.910
I always wanted to go in one!

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:23.800
So fast!

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.670
I got a strawberry one and a chocolate one.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:32.130
<i>Maybe Sophie-chan can eat sweets?</i>

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:45.440
You're still growing, 
so you need to eat more.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.190
You're not going to eat it?!

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:49.050
<b>Just wanted to order some.</b>

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:54.030
This is it.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.620
Thank goodness. We made it.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.080
<i>Oh, no! The parasol!</i>

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.450
Sophie-chan!

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.580
Are you okay, Sophie-chan?

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.790
Yeah, you saved me.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.050
I'm so glad.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:20.910
I thought you were going to die!

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.610
D-Don't cry!

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:25.740
I'm totally fine!

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:30.990
<i>A girl's tears are harder 
to deal with than the sun.</i>

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:37.650
The sun's finally gone down.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.880
It's good that we were able 
to get that autograph.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.610
It's all thanks to you, Akari.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:46.330
Huh?

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.290
Thank you.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:53.000
If you hadn't been there,

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:57.240
I would've had to go to the 
book signing without a head.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.220
Your work has blown my mind.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.880
Did you mean literally?!

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:03.190
So you would've gone even without a head.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.970
She might have been too scared 
to sign my book, though.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:12.100
<i>She's actually quite the immortal vampire.</i>

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.700
One more addition to my collection.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.590
<i>I wonder if she'll always 
remember this day, too.</i>

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:27.250
This is the day Akari saved 
me from the sunlight.

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:31.830
<i>I'm glad I could finally 
be a little help to her.</i>

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.050
Scary!

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:41.050
<i>The day Akari suddenly started 
to smile in a creepy way...</i>

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.520
<i>is probably how I'll remember this day.</i>

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.060
<i>My name is Natsuki Hinata.</i>

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:55.460
<i>Not too long ago, my friend 
Akari made a new friend,</i>

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.520
<i>and I guess she's living with her now.</i>

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.160
That reminds me.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:00.860
Huh?

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.880
Can I visit you at your new place sometime?

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.180
I wanted to meet your friend, too.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.470
<i>She's always had a flaky side,</i>

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:13.490
<i>so I worry if she's actually 
doing okay over there.</i>

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:16.920
<i>And who is this new friend, anyway?</i>

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:20.380
<i>They're "living together," 
so does that mean...</i>

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:26.260
<b>Imagine Imagine Imagine</b>

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.810
<i>It's not a guy, is it?</i>

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.260
Why don't you come over now, then?

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:27.850
Now?

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:29.840
J-J-Just wait a minute!

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:32.320
I want to go, but I have to mentally prepare!

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.960
Mentally prepare?

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:37.360
You're just visiting a friend. 
Don't be dramatic.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.400
I'll call first to make sure it's okay.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.570
<i>I mean, if it was really her 
boyfriend, it'd be a huge shock!</i>

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:46.310
Hey, Sophie-chan?

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:47.570
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.540
Oh, sorry. Were you sleeping?

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.580
Can I bring a friend over today?

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.780
<i>I don't mind.</i>

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:57.000
<i>Sounds like it's not a guy.</i>

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.800
<i>Actually, I didn't know you had friends.</i>

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.220
<i>I do!</i>

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:03.270
<i>There's Hinata-chan, who's coming today,</i>

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.260
<i>and I have two other friends.</i>

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.950
So three friends altogether?

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.540
Th-That many? That's too much!

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.970
<i>Four, counting you.</i>

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:15.250
Well, see you soon!

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.940
<i>Whoever it is, just how 
few friends do they have?</i>

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:26.890
Anxious

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:26.890
Anxious

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.950
Oh, Akari's friend is coming over.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.730
I need to prepare something.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:26.290
Like food and such...

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.870
<b>DVD/CD Rental</b>

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.870
<b>Big
Sale
Today</b>

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.650
Wait, isn't this the area where that...

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:33.720
Oh, they're having a sale today!

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:35.980
We could rent something 
and all watch it together!

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.080
Good idea!

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.790
<b>Recommended!!
Special Horror
Collection</b>

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.790
Just in

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.790
<i>That looks so scary!</i>

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.480
<i>I'm just gonna walk by 
without even looking at it.</i>

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:46.050
Oh, this is their recommendation!

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:49.670
Akari, shouldn't we get one of these?

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.720
Hinata-chan, are you scared?

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:57.220
N-No, I can watch stuff like that just fine!

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.290
I just didn't want you to be scared.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:02.050
Oh, okay! Then let's rent a whole bunch!

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:03.900
S-Sure!

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:08.760
<i>When I'm around her, I always end 
up acting tough for no reason.</i>

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.200
This is it!

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:19.370
It looks like a haunted house.

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:23.170
I'm home!

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.190
This is my friend, Hinata-chan.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:30.460
We've been friends since grade school.

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:32.430
It's nice to meet you.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.850
This is Sophie-chan.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.140
Doesn't she look just like a doll?

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:37.180
Nice to meet you.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.900
<i>She sounds younger than she did on the phone.</i>

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.700
<i>Her skin's so pale.</i>

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:47.280
<i>She's definitely pretty, but that 
doll-like vibe is a little scary.</i>

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:49.610
<i>Did she just laugh?</i>

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:53.800
<i>I was kind of worried when Akari said 
she wanted to bring a friend over,</i>

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.190
<i>but she looks like a normal person.</i>

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.580
<b>Was nervous.</b>

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.330
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:05.670
Hey... She doesn't have a reflection...

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:06.580
Yeah!

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.720
Sophie-chan is a vampire.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.270
Naturally, she has no reflection.

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:13.250
Oh, yeah. Of course.

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:17.890
<i>V-Vampire?!</i>

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.920
Well, no need to stand out here.
Why don't we go in?

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:25.530
Do you guys want some drinks?

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:26.610
Yes!

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:29.240
<i>She seems to be a friendly vampire.</i>

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:34.640
Um, thank you. You're so
considerate for your age.

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:39.050
She looks young, but she's 
actually 360 years old.

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:41.460
Don't bring up my age.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:47.060
Oh, uh... Sorry for being
so informal, Sophie-san.

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.960
Informal is fine with me.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:55.970
<i>Is Akari going to be okay, 
living with a vampire?</i>

00:15:56.710 --> 00:16:00.350
<i>She could be sucking her blood or something!</i>

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:05.850
Sophie-chan, you're looking 
cute as a doll, like always!

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.730
Hey! Stay back!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:11.590
Stop that, Akari! You're scaring her!

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:14.040
<i>Huh, what? It's the other way around?!</i>

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:19.090
I prepared a snack.
Have some, if you'd like.

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:20.790
Rice balls as a snack?

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:24.000
I thought humans liked rice balls.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.880
Let's eat!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:27.690
Let's eat.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:31.160
<i>Maybe it's like that thing with hamsters,</i>

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.840
<i>where people like feeding 
them sunflower seeds?</i>

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.430
Look, sunflower seeds!

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:41.440
Yup, humans and rice balls belong together.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:50.780
<i>Scary!</i>

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.020
Hinata-chan, do you have enough room?

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:56.690
I'm fine! I like small spaces.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.790
<i>But I don't want Akari to see me being pathetic,</i>

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.660
<i>so I have to be strong...</i>

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:07.370
This is so scary.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.640
These rice balls are so good.

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:11.990
<i>How come this isn't scaring Akari?</i>

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:14.080
Ghosts really are freaky.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:16.580
<i>And how come she's scared?</i>

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.640
<i>Vampires are monsters, too.</i>

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:27.140
<i>This girl seems like a scaredy-cat, too.</i>

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.610
<i>We might get along.</i>

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:32.360
That's such a waste of food!

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.580
<i>Guess I was wrong...</i>

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:37.950
That sure was scary, huh?

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:41.420
That reminds me, Sakuya was 
talking about a bunch of

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.540
scary rumors about this area.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.520
I mean, I don't particularly find it scary,

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:47.430
but there's this rumor about a doll mansion...

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:49.520
Oh, that's this house.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.130
<b>The Doll Mansion</b>

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:57.890
Apparently people mistakenly started that 
rumor about Sophie-chan and her house.

00:17:57.890 --> 00:18:00.140
Oh, really?

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.140
But there were so many others, too.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:06.270
Like the girl who wanders 
around the forest at night,

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:09.270
or the girl floating by the road...

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:13.690
I walk around this area a lot, 
but I've never seen her.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.510
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:19.070
<i>...they were all about Sophie-chan?</i>

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:23.790
<i>Now that I know that, 
I'm not really scared anymore.</i>

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:28.900
I didn't know there were rumors like that... 
Maybe I'll change my walking route.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:31.250
<i>She's the only one who doesn't get it.</i>

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.530
It's gotten late,

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.970
so why don't you eat dinner 
here and stay the night?

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.210
Good idea.

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:39.510
I won't say no to that.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.260
Then I'll go make dinner!

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.970
Uh, I'll help!

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:50.390
I think something's missing...

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:52.400
Why don't you add some kind of accent flavor?

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.770
<b>Blood Vessel</b>

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:54.780
Want to try this?

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:57.490
Uh, no, we won't be needing that.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.930
But this is good, domestic stuff.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.070
<i>Domestic doesn't change anything!</i>

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:08.220
Wow, this looks great!

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.470
Oh... Sophie, what are you having?

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:13.590
The only thing I eat is blood.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:14.890
Oh.

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:17.100
So we can't all eat the same meal.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:18.200
That's too bad.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.470
But tonight, I made tomato soup,

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:24.010
and I'm serving the ketchup like this.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.180
There you go!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.640
Blood-soaked style!

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:31.070
Now we can pretend we're eating with her!

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:32.880
<i>There goes my appetite...</i>

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.740
We're going to bed now.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.030
Goodnight!

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.090
Okay. Goodnight.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.300
I'm going to bed with you, too.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:04.300
Huh? But it's nowhere near your bed time.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.930
I mean, I'm happy, but...

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:08.670
This house is so dark.

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.390
The hallways and bathroom 
can get kind of scary.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.320
R-Really?

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.200
I mean, it doesn't bother me,

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:18.140
but if you need the bathroom
during the night, I'll go with you.

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:19.380
Really?

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:22.080
Then I guess the halls and 
bathroom won't be scary.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.160
Right?

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:31.560
<i>Wait, this is the scariest room in the house!</i>

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.700
You know, Sophie,

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:51.730
I was worried when I first heard that 
Akari was living with a stranger.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:55.440
But I'm relieved, now that I 
see her enjoying herself here.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.360
I mean, you're kinda weird, 
but you seem like a nice person.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:01.830
I'm not really weird.

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:06.750
I guess you really care about Akari, huh?

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.380
Y-Yeah, I do.

00:21:08.820 --> 00:21:11.160
We've been friends for a long time.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:16.040
Besides, Akari is so cute 
and girly and sweet.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:22.070
To me, she's sort of an idol, or an angel...

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:25.610
She can cook and sew, and she 
has so many womanly skills.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.470
I-I see...

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:30.990
You have strange preferences...

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:43.990
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:43.990
<b>The Vampire Goes to School</b>

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:07.700
Okay, we're going to school now.

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:10.450
Watch out for cars.

00:23:11.060 --> 00:23:12.450
Hey, Sophie...

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:15.620
I'll come over to visit again, okay?

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:17.970
Okay.

00:23:18.530 --> 00:23:20.330
Come over whenever you like.

00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:25.400
Isn't that great, Sophie-chan? 
You made another friend!

00:23:27.190 --> 00:23:31.300
But don't forget that I'm your best friend!

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:33.970
Just go to school already.

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:35.970
<i>Akari...</i>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:39.600
<i>You used to like me the most...</i>
